Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:59:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(app): the STEP bore's heavy test pins
 platform-robust facts

The bore's exact pins (one rings level at Z 20.000; 5530 / 5497 / 600)
never held on macOS: on the same commit ecb54b7f, macOS (Apple silicon)
plans 5786 / 5753 / 651 against the Windows measure, deterministically -
last-place platform float (most likely libm) under knife-edge planner
decisions (#882, #982), filed as #1010. Bisect on macOS puts the second
rings level (Z 10.000, crossing) at the #689 merge (STEP chord cap and
arc fit), which changed the bore's mesh and arcs and was not re-measured
in the heavy lane.

Every safety assertion stays: no verifier warning, no budget refusal,
every rings level named. The exact pins become: Z 20.000 goes to the
rings, a rings level only for a crossing, at most two of five levels on
the rings, arcs posted, 5000..=8000 moves with >= 98 % planar feeds.
Decision in docs/decisions/984-bore-heavy-pins.md.

Fixes #984

